          "properties": {
            "paragraphs": [
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What this is: ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1F4E79",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "A what-if calculator: what a lower speed would save in CO2, fuel cost and EU ETS cost, and what it costs in extra days at sea.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1B2A3A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "How to use it: ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1F4E79",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Move the sliders for speed change, carbon price and fuel price, and pick a speed relation. The cards recalculate at once for the selected year and segment.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1B2A3A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "textRuns": [
                  {
                    "value": "What to notice: ",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontWeight": "bold",
                      "color": "#1F4E79",
                      "fontSize": "11pt"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "value": "Annual MRV data show only a weak speed effect (the conservative case). The engineering rule gives the upper reference. The price is time: more days at sea per ship.",
                    "textStyle": {
                      "fontSize": "11pt",
                      "color": "#1B2A3A"
                    }
                  }
                ]
